+# Moussaoui: early checks, the August 24 update, and its testimony-substitute attachment
+
+Research date: October 30, 2026, America/New_York. This is an additive public-source review of court exhibits 326, 639 and 939, compared with the previously preserved 636/637. The [preceding review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/0b3d8f1448b9b7b78252e1a9c211a2599854d2af/investigation/broader-evidence/moussaoui-pending-link-requests-2026-10-29/README.md) identified 326 and 639 as unexamined candidate controls. This review follows those specific court links; it does not repeat the earlier searches or replace the original-record requirements.
+
+## What the new records add
+
+**The records preserve an assessment contrast, together with evidence of continuing investigative activity.** In exhibit 326, Samit reports flight-training circumstances he regards as suggestive of a hijacking plan, while acknowledging uncertainty. In 639, Maltbie later cautions against an earlier account suggesting planned wrongdoing, while reporting circulation of photographs and other information. The difference deserves a source-by-source comparison. Suspicion of a possible plan and lack of a specified indication of an actual plan are not automatically logically incompatible propositions. The sources do not reveal enough of their inputs to adjudicate why the assessments differ.
+
+The new PDFs are official court-hosted representations. Their hashes identify the downloaded bytes; neither hosting nor a hash authenticates a native message, its full attachments, transport, recipient receipt, or every assertion it contains. All three originals and the held predecessors are preserved unchanged. [SOURCES.json](SOURCES.json) supplies URL, access time, byte count and SHA-256; [SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json) supplies exact physical-page and paragraph anchors for the readings below.
+
+## 1. Exhibit 326 belongs to an earlier inquiry
+
+The [one-page 326 scan](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/326.pdf#page=1) displays an Abbott reply dated August 16, 2001, quoting Samit's August 15 message. Samit requests short-notice checks, describes reported flight training and his hijacking concern, acknowledges that the situation is not yet understood, and discusses possible immigration action. Abbott says he intends to write something that day, try to take it to a redacted recipient by the next day, and obtain the EC through ACS when written. That is a stated intended action, not a verified delivery, completed check or returned intelligence report. Pins R01–R02.
+
+The displayed dates are important: this is **not automatically a reply to the August 24 request in 637**. Similar short-notice subject matter does not establish a native thread or attachment join. The previous queue called it a candidate; it did not establish that join. Native headers, the EC, the proposed write-up and recipient/return records remain TODOs. No elapsed-time or timezone reconstruction is attempted.
+
+## 2. Exhibit 639 pairs dissemination reports with a caution
+
+The [one-page 639 scan](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/639.pdf#page=1) displays Maltbie's August 24, 2001, 5:29 PM reply to a quoted 7:19 AM update inquiry. Its first body paragraph says London and Paris Legats had received photographs and biographical information earlier that week and had been asked to seek identification/background information. The second reports that pocket-litter material was sent to Frahm that day, with a request for onward transmission, and that photographs were forwarded that afternoon. It promises additional information when obtained. These are **the sender's reports of transmission and tasking**, not recipient-side proof of receipt, analysis or a substantive return. Pin R03.
+
+The third body paragraph cautions that there was **“no indication”** of plans for wrongdoing and refers to a different impression apparently conveyed in an earlier communication. The earlier communication is not identified. Do not silently select 326, 636, 637 or any other exhibit as its referent. Pin R04.
+
+Beside that caution, preserve [636's August 24 possible-link report](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/636.pdf#page=1) and [637's August 24 field disagreement](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/637.pdf#page=1). In 636, Samit attributes a possible bin Laden connection to CIA/CTC assistance and French information. In 637, he reports the headquarters position on criminal/FISA sufficiency, expressly disagrees, seeks a firmer association and describes urgency. Neither source independently establishes the intelligence, the actual legal-review package or the original advice. Pin R05.
+
+These are different dated assessments, attributed assistance claims and reported actions. They remain side by side. The later August 28 drafting and legal-review accounts in the preceding review also remain intact; they are not newly reread or adjudicated here. The 639 caution does not erase the earlier field concern, and the earlier concern does not prove that the caution was knowingly false.
+
+## 3. Exhibit 939 provides explicit context, not another independent email
+
+The [939 PDF](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/939.pdf#page=1) consists of **four numbered testimony-substitute pages plus an attached fifth physical page**. Page 1 identifies it as a substitution for testimony of the pseudonymous witness John. Page 4 displays agreement by counsel and the date March 11, 2006. It is a retrospective agreed substitute, not a native 2001 email or a verbatim live-testimony transcript. Pin R06.
+
+The Moussaoui section on physical page 3, continuing onto page 4, describes an August 24 update inquiry and Maltbie's response. It places the inquiry in work on the requested FISA search and expressly identifies **exhibit 639 as the attached copy**. Physical page 5 is that email representation. This is a stronger document-association pointer than similar titles alone. The narrative's account is reported as its own source assertion; it is not permission to reconstruct masked fields in the scan. Pins R06–R07.
+
+Manual comparison of standalone 639 with 939 physical page 5 found the same visible sender/date/subject, three body paragraphs, quoted inquiry and substantive caution. The exhibit-stamp appearance, image scale/layout and overprinting differ. Multiple production marks are visible; faint characters were not reconstructed or used as identity keys. **No substantive wording difference was detected in the visible email portions inspected.** This is a bounded visual comparison, not pixel identity, native-message identity, forensic authentication or a finding about obscured text. Both PDF entities retain their separate hashes. The repeated attached email and the narrative discussing it must not be counted as independent confirmations of the email's historical truth. Pin R07.
+
+The remaining background on pages 1–3 concerns earlier Malaysia/Cole inquiries. It was read for context, including the source's limits on recollection and reported efforts to obtain/pass information. It is not presented as a newly established broader CIA theory or a completed investigation of the underlying May/July emails. Pin R08.
+
+## What to test next; what could weaken a suppression interpretation
+
+The useful lead is the **basis and distribution of the differing assessments**. Retrieve the exact earlier communication referenced in 639, the underlying French/CIA/UK information, the packets actually before each author/reviewer, and the native task/response/receipt chain. Then compare actual included assertions and contemporaneous reasons, without treating reported advice as the original legal record.
+
+Untested possibilities include a different information set, changed information, a distinction between suspicion and supported intent, different questions or thresholds, or unsupported downplaying. The records needed to distinguish these have not been obtained here. Actual knowing exclusion or misstatement of material information would strengthen a suppression interpretation; accurate caution about tentative information, inclusion elsewhere, or substantive follow-up could weaken it. None is selected as the cause. The same messages' reported dissemination, inquiries and continuing requests are contrary evidence to a blanket claim that investigative work stopped. Reports from the same sender and the same email reproduced in two exhibits do not become independent corroboration through document counts.
+
+## TODOs and reading limits
+
+[OPEN-TODOS.json](OPEN-TODOS.json) retains all **DRAFT-T01–T06**, with specific updates rather than silently marking the missing native inputs complete. The next untried indexed controls are **336/337**; they are not acquired or read in this review. Exact package association must be established before treating them as a missing attachment or an input to a particular decision. The August 15/16 EC/write-up/receipt, the unidentified earlier communication, underlying task returns, original advice, actual warrant/referral/nonreferral/order/return and native assembly history remain open.
+
+All eighteen original requirements across FAA, telephone, recorder, materials and steel tracks remain open or partial. This collateral lead neither replaces them nor completes the substantive investigation. No requested original is inferred to exist or be absent merely because these PDF containers expose no embedded attachment.
+
+**Actually read:** all seven physical pages in the three new PDFs, visually at the preserved render resolution; the two held single pages of 636/637 were reinspected. No other prior full source was newly read. Structural/integrity checks cover these five PDFs and the downloaded index. No hidden text extraction, OCR, masked-text reconstruction, native email/transport authentication, underlying-intelligence validation, legal adjudication or historical intent finding was performed. The report uses physical PDF pages and printed paragraph/header anchors, not invented source line numbers. Report line ranges in SOURCE-PINS locate our prose only.
+
+[CHECKLIST.md](CHECKLIST.md) accounts for the user's instructions. [TEXT-CHANGES.diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff) is the exact addition of these research text files against their immediately preceding absent state; earlier reports are unchanged, not replaced. [SOURCE-CHECKS.json](SOURCE-CHECKS.json) records actual preservation/structure checks. Those checks validate reference integrity, not historical conclusions or the truth of manual readings. Raw scans/rasters, full OCR, signatures, personal/contact/passport details, private correspondence and litigation strategy are excluded from this public derivative. No outreach, fee, new request/filing, mailbox access, deletion, private push, merge or history rewrite is part of this review. Publication verification follows the frozen candidate; it is distinct from source reading and substantive acceptance.
